    "created_at": "2021-01-26T09:39:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-01-26T09:39:17Z",
    "body": "> Possible explanation: \"bad\" character U+FCB5 is \"Arabic Ligature Dad with Hah Initial Form\", while the \"good\" character is \"Undefined in Unicode\". Since Arabic is right to left, that might explain the issue, yet it is unclear why only the combination PuTTY with Starship shows the issue.\r\n\r\nI think that's the most likely cause of this issue.\r\nThis is ultimately caused by #2009. According to https://github.com/Alexays/Waybar/issues/628 you might be able to work around your particular issue with a \"[unicode left-to-right mark](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Left-to-right_mark)\". The issue only appearing in Putty is likely caused by different text rendering stacks.\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
